      "extract": "Let $K$ be a knot and $J_{N}(K; q)$ be the usual $N$th colored Jones polynomial, normalized to be $1$ for the unknot. It is often useful to determine a $q$-hypergeometric expression for $J_{N}(K; q)$, and such expressions have been computed for a variety of knots (e.g., [@habiro; @hikami1; @hikami2; @thang; @masbaum; @walsh]). These have applications to the AJ conjecture [@hikami1], the generalized Volume conjecture",
      "extractCut": true
    },
