      "extract": "We begin by recalling the setup from [@takata]. Let $l$ and $t$ be coprime odd integers with $l > t \\geq 1$ and $p^{\\prime} := \\frac{l-1}{2}$. For $1 \\leq j \\leq p^{\\prime}$, define integers $r(j)$ such that $r(j) \\equiv (2j-1)t \\pmod{2l}$ and $-l < r(j) < l$. We put $\\sigma_j := (-1)^{\\lfloor \\frac{(2j-1)t}{l}\\rfloor}$, $r^{\\prime}(j) := \\frac{\\mid r(j) \\mid + 1}{2}$ and $i_{r^{\\prime}(j)}=j$ (and thus $i_k = j$ if",
